kyle cooper is a senior with a 3.8 grade  point average his declared major is  accounting and he intends to pursue a  career as a public or corporate  accountant at Hillsdale he plays on the  charger basketball team and assists with  the Hillsdale County Career access  planning project kyle is the second of  three children his younger sibling is a  university sophomore and his older  sibling is a University graduate the  family lives in northville michigan his  father is a real estate manager for ITC  holdings and his mother is self-employed  hello class of 2019 and welcome to  Hillsdale College as dr. Whalen  introduced I am Kyle Cooper I'm a member  of the men's basketball team and I'll be  entering my second year as a team  captain I am also an accounting major  which I understand sometimes comes with  a connotation that I may be a boring  person and I know it's been a long day  so I'll do my best to not be too boring  first of all I would like to acknowledge  what an honor it is to be speaking to  all of you today as you begin your  college careers as I thought about what  to say to all of you as well as your  parents I began to think about my own  time as an incoming freshman I received  a lot of advice from a lot of different  people learn to manage your time try not  to procrastinate build relationships  with your professors and administrators  and so much more that I'm sure a lot of  you have already heard you should know  that all that advice is more true than  you may even realize at this time though  it is not always easy to put into  practice as evidenced by the fact that I  still struggle with procrastination  because if we're being honest sometimes  watching the football game is more  attractive than writing a paper but  again it is good advice and I promise  the more disciplined you become the  better off you will be in your time at  college  by taking responsibility for your  actions and your grades they might be  difficult but it's not always the  professor's fault authority over your  own decisions and more importantly  accountability for the results of those  decisions the more likely you are to  experience success and that's what a lot  of advice tends to be focused on isn't  it how to get good grades earn a high  GPA build a good resume for your career  after college the quote-unquote success  I don't mean to take away from success  in the classroom at college because it  is a fundamental part of helping to open  some doors after school but speaking  from my own experience as a freshman I  remember feeling that the advice i was  given began to turn college into this  big game excuse the athletic reference a  contest where the winners leave happy  and the losers regretful please do not  ever let college or your life for that  matter turn into that people look at a  high school graduation class as you were  a few months ago or a group of incoming  college freshman as you are today and  it's easy for them to say you are the  future you are the next generation of  doctors lawyers politicians and so on  now I to believe that this freshman  class as well as all classes from  Hillsdale College will have an impact on  our country's future but today I'm  encouraging each of you not to look past  the steps that lead to that point but  rather to focus your attention on each  individual step waking up each day with  the determination to make that single  day great can have a profound impact on  your time here mistakes are always the  best learning material so I'd like to  offer you one of mine as a teaching  point see as a freshman when I was in  your  news I allowed myself to go through the  motions I woke up I went to class  practice dinner homework and studying  and back to bed day after day I did this  and it was that discipline that allowed  me to have some success here but I found  myself at the end of my freshman year  not having truly enjoyed college very  much I reflect on that experience and  realized that while I was disciplined  and that is a very important trait for  success I had become stagnant and that's  something that I wish to help all of you  avoid there's no staying the same you're  either improving or falling behind it's  a quote that I've heard a lot in sports  but it easily translates into all walks  of life use college to push your  boundaries learn to make time in one day  to go to class to get your homework done  participate in a grouper club call your  parents again this is you learning from  my mistakes and even hang out with your  friends in the dorm at night we are at a  very small college as I'm sure all of  you know allow the people here to become  a second family it's so easy to go  through today and make acquaintances  with the people you see wave hello as  you pass by smile it's a lot harder to  sit down or stand with someone and  expose yourself and have a true  conversation and make true friendships  but I promise you relationships are more  important in this life than any grade  you will receive in your four or five  years here carry yourself in a way that  you can be proud of every day focus on  all those little things that make each  day special really get to know the  people here and trust me there's a lot  of great ones and I promise you will  enjoy your college experience  congratulations on beginning a new stage  in life  and welcome to Hillsdale College
 

